          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00FFFF] transition-colors leading-snug mb-3">
            How to Pre-Sort DSLR RAW Files for Siril Stacking in Under 60 Seconds
          </h2>
          <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6 font-normal">
            Siril's automated scripts require strict <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/lights</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/darks</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/flats</code>, and <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/biases</code> subdirectories. Learn how to separate hundreds of raw exposures mathematically using 2D scatter plots.
          </p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[#00FFFF] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">
            <span>Read Full Guide</span>
            <span>&rarr;</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <!-- Guide 2: Culling Ruined Subs -->
        <a href="/software/astroplot/blog/how-to-cull-ruined-astrophotography-subs" class="group block rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#101726]/80 p-6 sm:p-8 no-underline hover:border-[#00FFFF]/50 hover:bg-[#131d31] transition-all shadow-xl">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="inline-block rounded-md border border-[#00FFFF]/30 bg-[#00FFFF]/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-[#00FFFF]">
              Subframe Quality &amp; Culling
            </span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-400">6 min read</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00FFFF] transition-colors leading-snug mb-3">
            How to Cull Bad Astrophotography Frames Fast Without Squinting at Thumbnails
          </h2>
          <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6 font-normal">
            Stop wasting 45 minutes manual-blinking 400 heavy RAW files. Learn why sigma clipping cannot fix cloud haze, and how to pinpoint ruined exposures in seconds on a 2D coordinate plot.
          </p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[#00FFFF] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">
            <span>Read Full Guide</span>
            <span>&rarr;</span>
          </div>
        </a>

        <!-- Guide 3: DSS vs Siril -->
        <a href="/software/astroplot/blog/deepskystacker-vs-siril" class="group block rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#101726]/80 p-6 sm:p-8 no-underline hover:border-[#00FFFF]/50 hover:bg-[#131d31] transition-all shadow-xl">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="inline-block rounded-md border border-[#00FFFF]/30 bg-[#00FFFF]/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-[#00FFFF]">
              Software Comparison
            </span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-400">7 min read</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white group-hover:text-[#00FFFF] transition-colors leading-snug mb-3">
            DeepSkyStacker (DSS) vs. Siril: Which Stacking Tool Fits Your RAW Workflow?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6 font-normal">
            An objective head-to-head comparison for DSLR and mirrorless astrophotographers. Compare 32-bit floating point precision, photometric color calibration, and raw file intake pipelines.
          </p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-[#00FFFF] group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">
            <span>Read Full Guide</span>
            <span>&rarr;</span>
